# Type arms over a trait value: `.Square(q)` tests the type
# the trait value holds and binds that value in place; the arm names a type
# as type position names it, and the table has an `else`. arms.jet: declared
# types and a builtin implementer (`impl Int.Shape`), an arm with no binding,
# a statement table and a value table. qualified.jet: another module's type
# through its module (`.geo.Point(p)`) beside this module's own `Point`.
# generic.jet: an arm that spells a generic's arguments (`.Box<Int>(b)`)
# checks.
fixture: TraitValueTypeArms.fixture
step arms: jet run arms.jet
exit: 0
stdout: = "square 3\na rect\nlabel hello\nshape 12\nint 7\n4\n0\n"
step arms_o0: jet run -O0 arms.jet
exit: 0
stdout: == arms
step arms_o2: jet run -O2 arms.jet
exit: 0
stdout: == arms
step qualified: jet run qualified.jet
exit: 0
stdout: = "geo point 7\nother line\n1\n"
step qualified_o2: jet run -O2 qualified.jet
exit: 0
stdout: == qualified
step generic: jet check generic.jet
exit: 0
